Remaining work (verified against the current runtime + compiler):

* AnyPointer: a set/non-nil AnyPointer field is not encoded as a pointer and is
  never decoded (an unset AnyPointer round-trips as nil, which works). Needs an
  opaque-pointer representation + sub-message copy to be complete.
* packing/unpacking: the stream codec is unpacked only; packed serialization is
  not implemented in the Lua runtime.
* old-format compatibility: lua/schema_zap.lua is a stale generated artifact and
  does not round-trip a CodeGeneratorRequest from a current ZAP compiler;
  regenerate it once packed/AnyPointer land.
* multiple input files in one compile invocation.
* performance tuning (e.g. precompute new_tab argument hints in generated code).
